tegers that lie in the interval $I.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nA={…,-3,-2}\\cup {2,3,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. If $q\\in Q,$ the solutions to $|4q|\\ge 8$ are all the rational numbers that lie in the interval $I.$ Since any real interval of nonzero length contains infinitely many rational numbers, it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊂C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,B,$ and $C.$\"" 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375998 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375999 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376000 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376001 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376002 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1041 "selection" 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376000 13194139535948 true] [17592186375997 1110 #uuid "36966bc3-5d59-5b84-8ba4-bfd82f50b6ac" 13194139535948 true] [17592186375998 1034 "None of the sets are infinite" 13194139535948 true] [17592186375998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535948 true] [17592186375998 1111 #uuid "aac83288-6e9d-58c1-a4fe-1829bdf94b35" 13194139535948 true] [17592186375999 1034 "$A$ only" 13194139535948 true] [17592186375999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535948 true] [17592186375999 1111 #uuid "57f41e3b-6996-5513-a0b1-0ead33ca562b" 13194139535948 true] [17592186376000 1034 "$A,B,$ and $C$" 13194139535948 true] [17592186376000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535948 true] [17592186376000 1111 #uuid "d527f2c5-b039-5849-a01b-a61d514a6452" 13194139535948 true] [17592186376001 1034 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139535948 true] [17592186376001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535948 true] [17592186376001 1111 #uuid "e4625fb5-d3f8-5097-9fd2-eb7baa0f296c" 13194139535948 true] [17592186376002 1034 "$C$ 